Slide 3 — Proposed 2027 UK Resi strategy / decision request

Create a dedicated recommendation/strategy slide.

The proposed framework is:

~£2bn total UK Resi commitments

Indicatively:

* ~£500m Together
* ~£500m Pepper
* ~£500m Enra
* ~£500m capacity for a fourth originator, sponsor-backed portfolio opportunity or other attractive platform

Frame this as approximately 4 core platforms plus optional capacity for sponsor / portfolio opportunities, rather than an immutable allocation if that reads better.

The strategy should allow rotation/churn over time rather than assuming the same four names indefinitely.

The objective is to preserve a scalable UK Resi franchise capable of generating approximately £10–15m revenue, rather than allowing MFG to become a c.£3m run-off business.

Explain the franchise benefits succinctly:

* sustainable client relevance;
* public RMBS arranging / left-lead opportunities;
* structuring capability;
* distribution capability and market intelligence;
* Sales & Trading / Syndicate connectivity;
* ability to compete for sponsor portfolio purchases and call-option/refinancing opportunities;
* ability to build into additional products and asset classes over time.

Make clear that breaking into a new originator is slow. Existing experience suggests it can take approximately 2–3 years to establish sufficient track record/trust and wait for existing warehouse revolving periods/refinancing windows. Therefore, exiting an established core relationship cannot be assumed to be immediately replaceable with another platform.

The proposed strategy should initially remain focused on UK Resi, rather than attempting to rebuild every MFG asset class simultaneously.

